    "finding": "Of twelve settlements, ten use the fused Defranceschi and two the spaced De Franceschi. The fused form appears on both sides of the pre-1797 border — seventeen of the nineteen families in formerly Venetian territory use it. What is one-directional is the spaced form: it occurs only in former Venetian territory, never in the Habsburg interior. Not a border you can draw, but a survival you can point at."
